      "author_association": "OWNER",
      "body": "## Objective\n\nEstablish a verified publication guard that allows Symphony development branches to be pushed to GitHub without triggering an unintended Vercel production or preview deployment.\n\n## Owner authorization\n\nThis issue authorizes:\n\n- Read-only inspection of the GitHub–Vercel connection and deployment history.\n- Determination of why commit 4919ab4 produced a failed Production-named deployment.\n- Identification of production, preview and branch deployment triggers.\n- Creation of the narrowest reliable guard preventing `codex/**` and `symphony/**` branches from deploying.\n- A harmless branch-only verification containing no application changes.\n- Documentation of configuration, evidence and rollback.\n- GitHub and Vercel configuration changes strictly necessary for this guard.\n\n## Required result\n\nProve that an authorized Symphony development branch can be pushed to GitHub without creating either a Vercel production or preview deployment.\n\nIf Vercel access is unavailable, configuration ownership cannot be verified, or the guard cannot be proven, stop as blocked before pushing application code.\n\n## Prohibited\n\n- Production deployment.\n- Application or database implementation.\n- Merge to main.\n- DNS or firewall changes.\n- Supabase changes.\n- Provider activation.\n- Paid-resource activation.\n- Credential exposure.\n- Weakening repository protection.\n- Pushing existing application work before the guard passes.\n\n## Validation\n\nReturn:\n\n1. Existing GitHub–Vercel relationship and triggering rules.\n2. Cause and classification of the failed deployment associated with 4919ab4.\n3. Exact guard selected and why.\n4. Configuration changes made.\n5. Harmless test branch and commit.\n6. Evidence that no Vercel deployment was created.\n7. Rollback procedure.\n8. Remaining risks.\n9. Confirmation that no application code, production deployment, Supabase mutation, DNS change or paid service was involved.\n\nOn success, remove `symphony-ready` and `symphony-running`, add `human-review`, and leave the issue open for owner acceptance.\n\nOn failure, remove execution labels, add `symphony-blocked`, and report the exact owner action required.\n",
      "closed_at": null,
      "closed_by": null,
